# Nothing lands on main except by merging a reviewed pull request.
#
# The same rule is enforced for Claude Code sessions by .claude/hooks/guard-bash.mjs, which
# catches it before the command runs and can explain itself. This one is git's own hook, so
# it also covers Codex, a plain terminal, and a human — the way commit-msg and pre-commit do.
# Both call one definition, so a session and a bare `git push` cannot disagree.
#
# Client-side, therefore bypassable with --no-verify. GitHub branch protection is the layer
# that is not; this is the fast one in front of it.
#
# Deliberate override: ALLOW_PUSH_TO_MAIN=1 git push ...
node .claude/scripts/check-push-target.mjs --pre-push
